    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS, 1 test). The change is complete and green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier rule: an owner's `membershipTier` is `'GOLD'` when their household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3+ members after the create; otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules still apply.\n\nChanges, following the existing \"fixed at creation time\" idiom used for the other derived owner fields:\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `householdSize` field (`household_size` column) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, after the household-id assignment, record the household size: `householdMembers.size() + 1` when the owner joins a shared household (non-null `householdId`), otherwise `1`. This is fixed at creation time, matching `namesakeCount`, `customerCode`, etc.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 updated the `membershipTier` expression to return `GOLD` when `householdSize >= 3`, else fall through to the existing SILVER/BRONZE derivation (so SILVER/BRONZE remain dynamically derived from `namesakeCount`/`email` as before).\n\n4. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `household_size` column to the `owners` table in all four schemas.\n\n5. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `membershipTier` description to document the GOLD rule.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold` test passes, and the full suite builds green.\n\nI chose the fixed-at-create approach (storing the size) over re-deriving it at read time deliberately: the spec says \"after **this** create,\" so the third member is GOLD while the first two \u2014 whose households had only 1 and 2 members at their own create time \u2014 correctly are not, even though all three now share the household.",
